$NetBSD$

Fix wrong kanji, wrong readings and malformed part-of-speech tags.

The conversions corrected here give a different word from the one the reading
asks for:

	げんかんしょうめい	玄関証明	-> 玄関照明
	こうかいはんてい	高階判定	-> 公開判定
	しょうかようすい	消化用水	-> 消火用水
	ひなんじゃくしゃ	非難弱者	-> 避難弱者
	ひなんたいろ		非難退路	-> 避難退路
	ゆまくいじょう		油膜以上	-> 油膜異常
	ぜんきょくろくおん	歩道整備	-> 全曲録音

The last one had been given the entry for a different word entirely; 歩道整備
is added back under its own reading, ほどうせいび.

Two readings were wrong: あいずしっき for 会津漆器, which is あいづ, and
かんすいきんぞく for 関水金属, which is せきすい.  Several entries were
missing the # of their part-of-speech tag, or carried #35 or #T#5 where #T30
was meant, and were therefore ignored.

Fedora has carried these since 2010, and anthy-unicode -- the fork that is
still maintained -- has every one of them.  anthy itself has not been
released since 2009, so there is nowhere upstream to send them.

